      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "white_genocide_claim",
      "label": "White Genocide Claim",
      "description": "A false and hateful narrative that falsely claims the South African national flag represents a genocidal intent against white South Africans. This is a racially charged conspiracy theory that has been used to incite xenophobia and racial hatred, often by white supremacist groups or individuals promoting apartheid-era ideologies. It is not based on historical fact and is widely condemned as hate speech.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_4957aef4"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a0944a62",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "South_Africa",
      "label": "Republic of South Africa",
      "description": "A country in Southern Africa with a history of apartheid, racial segregation, and post-apartheid reconciliation. The national flag symbolizes the unity of its diverse racial and cultural groups. The claim that it represents 'white genocide' is a distortion of its true meaning and history.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
